<title>MEXICO: Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 9.</title>
<headline>Mexican daily port, shipping update for July 9.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Mexican ports were open on Wednesday, the Communications and Transport Ministry (SCT) said in its 1000 local/1500 GMT daily meteorological report.</p>
<p>The ministry said Hurricane Dolores winds had relaxed to between 70 and 85 knots (133 km/77 miles and 162 km/94 miles) and continued to head west, away from Mexico's Pacific coast. Ships were still advised not to sail near the hurricane, about 920 miles (1472 km) west-southwest of southern Baja California.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
